{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"2335eaf41e5b6dfee3a51cd2d7a2106d810ab6b607508dddacd5308be8bde5bd","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_a56098d8524db7a644c9633aa2803dafb69fdb3a5ba14ba1a5cac4150e2fceb8","overall_assessment":"The paper explicitly addresses ethical considerations related to gender bias in machine translation, proposing a method to mitigate these biases through neuron control. It utilizes the United Nations parallel corpus, a standard public dataset, without specific disclosures regarding consent or licensing terms. The submission adheres to double-blind review conventions by anonymizing author identities. The provided text does not contain evidence of plagiarism or dual submission, nor does it include a dedicated broader impact statement or specific compliance checklists beyond the ethical discussion of bias.","paper_id":"H1z-PsR5KX","paper_identity_sha256":"8563781e21528b458f804fa1196fd9ff6348682d215559bd7dfb164e86a7de47","prompt_identity_sha256":"fb413983ab3b0e89b3d5c796a8d9c026738f16aa6ed9d86a8a2294a8d24bee3b","raw_response_sha256":"17f2e636d47348597b96e0a890152b0effd62903227dcb181a2cd73b45bd26c3","request_identity_sha256":"b822631cd2a5c15597e0e0a16c659d20e1b11a7936e8de43d50d914e2083a3fa","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"add01a5133f933d81c362f063222a06d19786d5f332829b0fdf74816ed9c6ee0","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-028","SRC-030"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly addresses ethical concerns regarding gender bias in neural machine translation. The authors identify that MT systems often reflect gender stereotypes, such as associating doctors with men and nurses with women, and propose a method to control translation output to mitigate these biases. They demonstrate the ability to modify neuron activations to change gendered translations, although they note that controlling gender is more difficult than controlling tense or number, with a success rate of 21%. This discussion provides a concrete pathway for addressing potential harms related to bias in automated translation systems.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-015"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes the United Nations (UN) parallel corpus for all experiments, training models on 500K sentences per target language. The UN parallel corpus is a widely used public dataset in the field. The paper does not provide specific details regarding data consent, privacy compliance, or the specific licensing terms under which the UN corpus is used. However, the use of this standard public resource for research purposes is consistent with common practices in the field, and no privacy violations or misuse of restricted data are evident in the provided text.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper is submitted under double-blind review, as indicated by the header 'Anonymous authors' and 'Paper under double-blind review'. The text does not contain author names, institutional affiliations, or acknowledgements that would reveal the identities of the authors. The references and citations are standard and do not appear to contain self-identifying information that would compromise anonymity.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The provided paper text does not contain explicit disclosures of plagiarism, self-plagiarism, or dual submission. The content appears to be original work, with proper citations to prior research in the field of neural machine translation and interpretability. Without access to external plagiarism detection tools or submission history, it is not possible to definitively confirm the absence of textual overlap or simultaneous submission to other venues. However, no evidence of misconduct is visible in the supplied text.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-028"],"review_text":"The paper discusses the broader impact of its work in the context of mitigating biases in neural machine translation, specifically gender bias. This is integrated into the introduction and the section on controlling translations. However, the paper does not include a separate, dedicated 'Broader Impact' statement or a compliance checklist as is sometimes required by conferences. The discussion of societal impact is limited to the specific application of bias mitigation in translation, without a broader analysis of potential negative societal consequences or other ethical implications of the interpretability methods proposed.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"24a7579fe6884f5bcfd414a140448a8f2fba2477f5369c8f25718011e7becdfe","paper_id":"H1z-PsR5KX","paper_ordinal":100,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"17f2e636d47348597b96e0a890152b0effd62903227dcb181a2cd73b45bd26c3","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"H1z-PsR5KX","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"a6ab8d4e082db9e8892b398f01e71daf8c7fe6363f0cda9802b9ac38fcbb74c5","request_identity_sha256":"b822631cd2a5c15597e0e0a16c659d20e1b11a7936e8de43d50d914e2083a3fa","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":863,"prompt_tokens":19156,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":20019},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"b822631cd2a5c15597e0e0a16c659d20e1b11a7936e8de43d50d914e2083a3fa","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}